@*
    GcRootTree's sibling for when HeapAnalyzer.GetGCRoots throws outright, rather than completing
    with one of GCRootTree.Outcome's four states -- the same "an unreadable referent is a node, not a
    500" principle ObjectReferenceTreeBuilder.Unreadable applies to the object tree, applied here at
    whole-search granularity since gcroot has no per-node fetch to isolate the failure to (5.3, unlike
    5.4, computes the whole tree from one analyzer call).

    Reuses .dn-empty's layout -- this is functionally the same "nothing to show, and here is why"
    shape GcRootTree.cshtml's own Unrooted arm uses -- plus a danger badge so it reads as a failure
    rather than a legitimate empty result.
*@
@model DotNetDump.Web.Rendering.GCRootErrorModel

<div id="v-gcroot">
    <div class="dn-empty">
        <div class="dn-empty__title">
            <span class="dn-badge dn-badge--danger">could not resolve</span>
            Retention path for @Display.Address(Model.TargetAddress) could not be computed.
        </div>
        <div>@Model.Reason</div>
    </div>
</div>
